    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n16821" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">exercĭtōrĭus</span></b> ,
			a, um, adj.
		exercitor
		 (post-class.). <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Of</i> or <i>belonging to
			exercise</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">jacula,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Tert. Poenit. 12</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Of</i> or <i>belonging to trade</i>
			or <i>business</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">actio,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Dig.
				14</span></i>
			 tit. 1; <i><span class="en">ib. 1, 7</span></i>.</div>
